    "probe_text": "Here is the exact ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, traced through `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` and the service/entity layers it calls.\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Bean Validation of the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, interface is `@Validated`). Constraints, per field:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)` (nullable)\n   - `postcode` \u2014 no constraint (nullable)\n   - `registrationDate` \u2014 `@Valid` (nullable)\n   - `sharesHousehold` \u2014 no constraint (defaults to `false`)\n   \n   Any failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400** via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.\n2. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (when `petclinic.security.enable` is true).\n\n## Inside the controller body (in order)\n\n3. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** via MapStruct `ownerMapper.toOwner` (`id`, `pets`, `customerCode` ignored).\n4. **Normalize address** (`AddressNormalizer.normalize`: collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE). If result blank \u2192 **400**; else `owner.setAddress(normalized)`.\n5. **Normalize telephone to E.164** (`TelephoneNormalizer.toE164`, default country code 61, 8\u201315 digits). If empty/invalid \u2192 **400**. (Value assigned in step 10.)\n6. **Normalize email** (lower-case/trim). If non-null and `!isValid` \u2192 **400**.\n7. **Postcode check** \u2014 if postcode present and `!postcodeValidator.isValid(postcode, city)` \u2192 **400**.\n8. **Roll registration date** \u2014 `BusinessDay.rollForward(dto date or today())` (Sat/Sun \u2192 Mon); `owner.setRegistrationDate(...)`.\n9. **Daily cap** \u2014 `clinicService.countOwnersByRegistrationDate(date) >= 100` \u2192 **429**.\n10. **Assign** `owner.setTelephone(e164)` and `owner.setEmail(normalizedEmail)`.\n11. **Household sharing** \u2014 if `sharesHousehold == true`: `clinicService.shareHousehold(owner)` \u2014 generates a household id (SHA-256 of lastName+address), **backfills and saves existing household members' `householdId` (DB writes)**, and sets `owner.householdId`.\n12. **City cap** \u2014 `clinicService.countOwnersByCity(city) >= 50` \u2192 **409**.\n13. **Duplicate check** \u2014 `clinicService.existsOwnerByIdentityKey(owner.getIdentityKey())` (scans all owners, matches on the derived telephone/email/household key) \u2192 **409**.\n14. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** (`@Transactional`). For a new owner it sets, before saving:\n    - `customerCode` (if null) via `CustomerCodeGenerator` \u2192 `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`\n    - `namesakeCount` (case-insensitive first+last name count)\n    - `bulkSignupWarning` (registrations that day > 80)\n    - `householdSize`\n    - then `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.\n15. **On JPA insert** \u2014 `Owner.@PrePersist normalizeRegistrationDate()` fires again (defaults null \u2192 today, then `BusinessDay.rollForward`), and Hibernate re-runs entity Bean Validation: `@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone plus `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)` on telephone.\n16. **Audit log** \u2014 `ownerAuditLogger.logCreated(owner)` writes an `AUDIT` SLF4J line (id, customerCode, registrationDate).\n17. **Map back to `OwnerDto`** (`toOwnerDto`, computes `displayName = lastName + \", \" + firstName`; response also exposes derived transients).\n18. **Set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header** and return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- The **registration date is rolled forward twice** \u2014 once explicitly in the controller (step 8) and again in the entity's `@PrePersist` (step 15). Idempotent, but redundant.\n- There is **no email sending, push/notification, password encoding, or cache eviction** anywhere in this path. The only \"notification\"-like effect is the audit log line.\n- `shareHousehold` (step 11) mutates and persists *other* owners **before** the city-cap, duplicate, and save checks \u2014 so if the request is later rejected at step 12/13, those household backfill writes have already occurred within the transaction (they roll back with it, but they are a side effect of this request path).\n- The active profile is `spring-data-jpa`, so `SpringDataOwnerRepository` is the live repository; the JDBC/JPA impls are inactive.\n\nOne caveat: much of this trace comes from generated sources under `target/generated-sources/openapi` (the `OwnersApi` interface and `OwnerFieldsDto`), which reflect the current build output. The hand-written controller, service, entity, and validators are all under `src/main/java`."
